## Naive approach (and why it is biased)

A common approach in observational studies estimates the effect of vaccination via the Cox model
$$
\lambda(t | A, X) = \lambda_0(t) \exp(\beta_AA + \beta_X X)
$$

Applying this to our generated data above, we find:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
fit_naive <- coxph(
  Surv(time_new, status_new) ~ A + X,
  data = example_df |>
    mutate(time_new = pmin(time2, cens), status_new = ifelse(time2 <= cens, 1, 0))
)

tbl_regression(fit_naive)
```

